    "text": "A Get Well Note\n\nMiss Hall called the names on the class list, “Jane.” “Here!” “Quin.” “Here!” “Hope, Hope?” “She is still at home sick. She has a stuffed up nose, and a flushed face,” said Tate.\n\nQuin asked, “Can we make Hope a get well note?” Luke added, “Let’s bring Hope a stuffed dog as a get well gift.” “That is a fine plan,” said Miss Hall.\n\n“What should we write in the note?” asked Jane. The kids looked at Miss Hall for help. Miss Hall said, “To Hope. We want you to get well fast. We send you lots of hugs. We miss you. Best wishes. From, Miss Hall’s class.” Tate said, “You rocked it, Miss Hall!” The kids all missed Hope. They were pumped to send the note and gift."
